@startuml
!include _libcpg-theme.iuml
title Dense bit-set join — portable runtime dispatch and exact tail

start
:Receive equal-width `u64` slices\nand Union or Intersection; <<#DBE4FF>>
if (fewer than 8 words?) then (yes)
  :Scalar word loop\nupdate + exact changed flag; <<#FFE8CC>>
else (no)
  if (target is x86 or x86-64?) then (yes)
    :Read cached `OnceLock` decision; <<#E5DBFF>>
    if (runtime AVX2 detected?) then (yes)
      :Select largest prefix divisible by 4; <<#FFF3BF>>
      while (complete 4-word chunk remains?) is (yes)
        :Unaligned 256-bit loads; <<#DBE4FF>>
        :Bitwise OR or AND\ncompare old with new; <<#B2F2BB>>
        :Unaligned destination store\nOR lane result into changed; <<#C3FAE8>>
      endwhile (no)
      :Scalar loop over 0..3 tail words\nOR exact tail result into changed; <<#FFE8CC>>
    else (no)
      :Scalar word loop\nupdate + exact changed flag; <<#FFE8CC>>
    endif
  else (no)
    :Compile only scalar implementation; <<#FFE8CC>>
  endif
endif
:Return unchanged public lattice value\nand semantic change Boolean; <<#B2F2BB>>
stop

floating note right
  Subset is a separate scalar lane:
  it returns at the first word for which
  <latex>a_i \mathbin{\&} \neg b_i \ne 0</latex>.
end note

legend right
  |= colour |= role |
  |<#DBE4FF>| valid slice input / loads |
  |<#E5DBFF>| one cached runtime decision |
  |<#FFF3BF>| vector partition |
  |<#B2F2BB>| equivalent bitwise semantics |
  |<#C3FAE8>| exact store and change reduction |
  |<#FFE8CC>| portable scalar oracle and tail |
endlegend
@enduml
